        "findings": "VERDICT: CHANGES REQUESTED\n\nThe overall structure is a good fit for this codebase. Placing `getAgeBand()` as a `@Transient` derived getter on `Owner` mirrors the existing `getIdentityKey()` precedent (line 181), the field sits naturally beside `registrationDate`, the getter/setter follow the file's ordering, and the schema/OpenAPI additions are consistent with the surrounding columns/properties. The derivation belongs on the entity, and nothing is duplicated. Just one idiomatic nit:\n\n- **`Owner.java:142` \u2014 fully-qualified `java.time.Period` breaks the file's import convention.** Every other `java.time` type in this file is imported (`import java.time.LocalDate;` at line 24) and referenced by simple name throughout (`LocalDate.now()`, `LocalDate` fields, `toBusinessDay`). Introducing an inline `java.time.Period.between(...)` is inconsistent and slightly harder to read. Add `import java.time.Period;` and call `Period.between(this.birthDate, this.registrationDate)` to match the surrounding style."
